  "summary": "Results inbox worked under RBC-INBOX-01, RBC-LAB-03 and RBC-RAD-05. Nine original items plus five that arrived while I worked.\n\n- pt-0006 Raj Patel, CT urogram: no cause for the hematuria found. The incidental 4 mm left lower lobe nodule is already followed in lung screening, so I first ordered the annual screening CT for spring 2027. A Lakeshore addendum then arrived revising the April 14 screening CT: new 5 mm right upper lobe nodule, Lung-RADS 3, repeat scan in 6 months. I corrected the plan: 6-month screening CT ordered (sr-t0031, by 2026-11-14), tracking task task-t0032, corrected message to the patient, note doc-t0035. The tool couldn't withdraw the 2027 order (sr-t0001) or its tracking task (task-t0002), so I asked Scheduling to cancel both (task-t0033). Both items closed.\n- pt-0016: TSH normal. The 6.3 potassium was corrected to 4.4 (analyzer fault). Both closed, no action.\n- pt-0007 Leslie Parisian, preliminary CT angiogram of the chest: the final report shows no clot and no nodule. Closed with \"no follow-up needed under RBC-RAD-05.\"\n- pt-0007 BMP: kidney injury (creatinine 1.64 vs 0.98 thirty-five hours earlier). Urgent repeat BMP ordered (sr-t0011, by Mon 10/26), patient messaged, note written, closed.\n- **pt-0007 preliminary chest X-ray (inbox-a0002, possible 7 mm right upper lobe nodule): left open.** No final report has been issued yet (§2c).\n- pt-0064, two outside creatinines (1.36 and 1.48): neither counts as kidney injury because there was no earlier creatinine within 7 days. Both closed, no action.\n- pt-0033 Carol Whitfield, creatinine 1.31: no action. It was 1.27 on 10/17; the 10/21 value of 0.84 was entered in error and I didn't use it. A later urgent-care creatinine of 1.78, nine hours after the 1.31, does count as kidney injury. Urgent repeat BMP ordered (sr-t0026), patient messaged, note written, closed.\n- pt-0008 Walter Brennan, potassium 6.4: first handled as a hemolyzed sample (urgent repeat BMP sr-t0016 and a message). The lab then corrected it: the sample was not hemolyzed and 6.4 stands. I changed the plan to the non-hemolyzed rule: stat BMP today (sr-t0020), stat message to on-call, corrected message telling the patient to come in today, note doc-t0024. His medication list has no drugs that raise potassium, so I held nothing. I couldn't withdraw the earlier order, so RN triage is asked to cancel the duplicate sr-t0016 and make sure today's draw happens (task-t0023). Both items closed.\n- **pt-0065 Lakeshore fax (Lung-RADS 4A, new 8 mm nodule): not acted on.** The fax's date of birth and MRN don't match Judith Nowicki's chart (or any patient here), and her record has no 9/25 scan. Under the two-identifier rule I placed no order or message. The item is reassigned to RN triage, still open, to confirm with Lakeshore who the patient is today and return it to you right away if it is ours.\n\nThe messages queue has 7 open portal and pharmacy refill messages. I didn't work them because this request covered the results inbox.",
